//IO
strings.NewReader(s string)
bytes.NewReader(b []byte)

both of the above take a initial value
you can keep reading from them 
	all at once (or)
	n bytes 
they have 
	len() - length of the un-read bytes left
	size() - total length of the input given while creating this reader 

here, you can only read the initial string you have added 
you cannot add anything more to this  

// ------------
strings.NewBuilder -- this is nothing but writer 
you can keep writing into this 
// ------------
bytes.NewBuffer(s string)

here you can read the initial string & also can add extra byte on the go 
this is both reader and writer 

this cannot be used as buffer for large contents 

// ------------ buf io ----------
bufio.NewReaderWithSize(reader,10)
	size gives 10, the size of the buffer 
	buffered() gives how many byte that can be read from current buffer 
	create []byte of size 10 and read
	[]byte 20 & read will still read 10, if you want to read 20 (use ReadFull())

bufio.NewWriterWithSize(writer,10)
	write()
	flush()




